ame_id":"steam-5061040","kind":"announcement","title":"Level all, item tooltips, and a new storybook","summary":"Two things you asked for, a new storybook, and a rat that had grown far too big. Level all A new Level all button sits beside the buy multiplier at the top right. It spends your gold one level at a time, always on the lowest-level hero in your party, so the whole party climbs together for as long as your gold lasts. You no longer have to level each hero in turn. {STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/46257625/66a6c8c9d869b2132c19e783d0446ee2e609034f.jpg Item tooltips Hover over any item, in the bag or on a hero, to","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-24T08:33:41Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1847286114039126","verified_at":"2026-10-24T08:34:29Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5061040-1847286114033203","game_id":"steam-5061040","kind":"announcement","title":"Graphics settings, and a much faster room","summary":"This update is all about performance: Quartermark now runs comfortably on older laptops, and faster on every PC. Graphics settings Settings → Display now has Graphics: Auto, Low, Medium and High. Auto, the default, looks at your graphics card the first time you start the game and picks the setting that suits it: High on a gaming PC, Medium or Low on a laptop. If the game still runs slowly, Auto lowers itself one step and tells you. A setting you pick yourself is never changed. Low keeps every cr","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-22T15:30:36Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1847286114033203","verified_at":"2026-10-22T18:04:10Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5061040-1847286114029971","game_id":"steam-5061040","kind":"announcement","title":"A pink prestige button, and the bosses board first","summary":"A small update with a few things that make the climb easier to read. A full prestige, at a glance The prestige button on the top bar glows pink when a full prestige is ready: your climb has reached your record, and the reset pays all of its shards. {STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/46257625/c5b3a19e17ce0b5295115faa2404b459d1120adc.jpg {STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/46257625/6f3418e397500fe6682f674e56b651734d7e2b27.jpg The bosses board first The leaderboards now open on the bosses board, the first of the tabs. {STEAM_CLAN_","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-21T18:41:17Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1847286114029971","verified_at":"2026-10-21T20:30:47Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5061040-1846651706695599","game_id":"steam-5061040","kind":"announcement","title":"Companions, champions, and a prestige that is fair to everyone","summary":"The biggest update yet, and all of it is about the long climb: goals that stay with you through every reset, six small friends who walk with your party, every stat explained in numbers, and prestige rules that keep the leaderboards honest. {STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/46257625/506219a8211695560a3c08bff551ce62fa389e7a.jpg Companions Six young creatures of the deep — a mossy bear cub, a lilac batling, a hermit crablet in a pearl-lit shell, a frost pup, a temple jackal pup and an ember newt. They blink, look","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-20T14:55:15Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1846651706695599","verified_at":"2026-10-20T21:24:18Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5061040-1846651706693773","game_id":"steam-5061040","kind":"announcement","title":"Four new heroes, a Weekly Gate, and every boss fighting like itself","summary":"A big one. The full game gains four heroes and a hundred bosses that finally fight like the creatures they are; the demo gets the new systems, the fixes and every creature's own special attack. Four new heroes Stormcaller — Chain Lightning strikes every creature and pushes their attacks back, so a boss's special comes later. Witch — curses that weaken, a poison cloud that stops enemy healing, and a hush that silences a weakened creature's special. Bonecaller — a tank who drinks: his Marrow Drain","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-20T05:25:20Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1846651706693773","verified_at":"2026-10-20T21:24:18Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5061040-1846018067937374","game_id":"steam-5061040","kind":"announcement","title":"Ten bosses rebuilt, every hero worth playing, legendaries that mean something","summary":"This update reworks how the first ten bosses fight, how your party is balanced, and how rare the best loot is. Everything below is already in the demo. The bosses fight back Every boss in the demo has a new special attack, cast in the room's own light — and each one finally fits the creature casting it. The Honey Queen hurls globs of amber at your party and slows it. The Thorn Lord grows rows of thorns across the floor toward you. The Bog Giant brings both fists down into the marsh. The Root Wyr","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-10T21:50:49Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1846018067937374","verified_at":"2026-10-20T21:24:18Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"}],"analyses":[],"news_status":{"steam-5061040":{"last_attempt_at":"2026-10-26T16:46:58Z","status":"ok","all_sources_checked_at":"2026-10-26T16:46:57Z","error_code